From 40f5878436a373f3da6305adcb3823c888a80413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NOVA Delivery <nova-delivery@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:12:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] chore: promote the project to the git root so GitHub can
 see the workflow

The eighth upload (FastAPI-v15, 5ee0295) nested the whole project inside a
Final/ directory -- this time because the *workspace* folder was uploaded, not
just the repository. GitHub consequently reported zero workflows and zero runs:
.github/workflows/backend.yml sat at Final/.github/workflows/backend.yml, where
GitHub never looks. tools/check_layout.sh failed on it in 0.1s, as designed.

Promoted with tools/restructure_repo.sh (every move is a git mv, so history
follows the files). Also dropped .scratch/ -- two throwaway scripts from the
previous session that were swept up in the upload -- and kept the useful one as
tools/verify_delivery.sh, a real round-trip test of the release artefacts.
