-From 5be660787fcca79a1a8db9c5b90b3066872843e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: NOVA Delivery <nova-delivery@localhost>
-Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:16:31 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Make the release snapshot byte-reproducible
-
-git archive stamps the zip with the commit id (archive comment) and the commit
-time (member mtimes), so two commits with an identical tree produced different
-bytes. That made releases/SHA256SUMS.txt unverifiable in principle: committing
-the sums creates a new commit, so the recorded zip hash never matched the zip
-regenerated from that commit.
-
-tools/make_release.sh now normalises the metadata after git archive: fixed
-timestamp, sorted entries, no archive comment, tracked file modes preserved
-(tools/*.sh stay executable). The snapshot is a function of the tree alone.
