+```
+
+This time the consequence was **measured on GitHub itself**, not inferred. The API
+reports no workflow at all:
+
+```
+GET /repos/AbdElrhmanAhmed7/FastAPI-v15/actions/workflows → {"total_count": 0, "workflows": []}
+GET /repos/AbdElrhmanAhmed7/FastAPI-v15/actions/runs      → {"total_count": 0, "workflow_runs": []}
+```
+
+Zero workflows, zero runs: GitHub never even parsed `backend.yml`, because it sat at
+`Final/.github/workflows/backend.yml`. The same query against the previous repository
+returns one `active` workflow and one green run, which is the control for this
+experiment — both are recorded in `verification/2026-11-12-v15/github-actions.json`.
+
+Fixed with the tool built for exactly this, so history follows the files:
+
+```
+$ bash tools/restructure_repo.sh
+── wrapper detected: Final/ ─────────────────────────────────────────
+  git mv Final/.github .github
+  git mv Final/NOVA NOVA
+  …
+$ bash tools/check_layout.sh
+✓ layout ok – git root = project root, GitHub will run .github/workflows/backend.yml
+```
+
+`.scratch/` was dropped — workspace scratch, not project content. The useful half of
+it became **`tools/verify_delivery.sh`**, described below. The Arabic handover note was
+moved out of the tree for the same reason, and one more: `test_english_content.py`
+scans every text file in the repository, so an Arabic document at the root **fails the
+language gate**. It is delivered beside the repository, not inside it — repository
+documentation stays English, as §9.4 requires.
+
+#### The previous session's release step never actually ran
+
+Its documents were in the upload; its **artefacts were not**. The commit meant to
+carry them aborted with `Author identity unknown … fatal: unable to auto-detect email
+address`, and the session ended there. So this tree still carried the *v14* package,
+and all three delivery checks failed on arrival:
+
+| Check | Result on the tree as uploaded |
+| --- | --- |
+| `bash tools/check_layout.sh` | ✗ `NOVA/backend is not at the git root` |
+| `cd releases && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt` | ✗ `nova-backend-final.zip: FAILED open or read` — gitignored, so it never travels with a clone |
+| `git am releases/nova-backend-final.patch` | ✗ `patch does not apply` — its header is `From fd73e5a…`, and none of `24dc3e6`, `bbfa863`, `fd73e5a` exist in this squashed history |
+
+The git identity is now configured in the repository, the artefacts are regenerated
+above `5ee0295`, and — for the first time — both delivery routes were **executed**
+rather than described.
+
+#### A package is not a delivery until it has been applied
+
+`make_release.sh` proves the artefacts exist; `sha256sum -c` proves they are intact.
+Neither proves they *work*. `tools/verify_delivery.sh` now does, on throwaway clones:
+
+1. the checksums match the artefacts that are actually present;
+2. `git am` on a clean clone of the baseline reproduces the delivered tree file for
+   file, and the layout guard passes afterwards;
+3. the zip, extracted and uploaded as **contents**, passes the guard;
+4. the same zip uploaded as a **folder** is *rejected* by the guard — a negative test,
+   because a guard that never fails is not a guard.
